            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I can not reproduce with the following setup:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.files').setup()\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>et', function()\r\n  if not require('mini.files').close() then require('mini.files').open() end\r\nend)\r\n```\r\n\r\nExecuting `<Leader>et` toggles explorer (closes if shown, opens if not shown). Also opens it if explorer was previously closed with `q`.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nI am pretty confident that this is not an issue with 'mini.files'. If anything, it looks like this config loads 'neo-tree.nvim' which [has `<Leader>e` mapping defined in AstroNvim](https://github.com/AstroNvim/AstroNvim/blob/bcff9df3827a12bac776a400114a058f04d0d38c/lua/astronvim/plugins/neo-tree.lua#L10). So `<Leader>e` toggles 'mini.files' only once after which it seems to be overridden to toggle Neo-tree.",
